 This method takes optional arguments ``pk=``, ``column_order=``, ``foreign_keys=``, ``not_null=set()`` and ``defaults=dict()`` - explained below.
 
+Creating STRICT tables
+----------------------
+
+SQLite 3.37.0 introduced `STRICT tables <https://www.sqlite.org/stricttables.html>`__,
+which reject values that cannot be losslessly converted to the declared column
+type. Pass ``strict=True`` when explicitly creating a table::
+
+    db["events"].create(
+        {"id": int, "name": str, "score": float},
+        pk="id",
+        strict=True,
+    )
+
+The option can also be passed to ``insert()``, ``insert_all()``, ``upsert()``,
+``upsert_all()`` or ``lookup()`` when those methods create a new table. Use
+``table.strict`` to check if an existing table is strict.
+
